      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the limit is lower for extended-release. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nHere are some options within the label:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day), a common target dose.\n- **A lower starting dose**, such as 500 mg once or twice daily, titrated up if the patient is new to metformin.\n\nIf 1700 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, I can enter it as 850 mg twice daily. Tell me which regimen you want, and whether the formulation is immediate-release or extended-release, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
