      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, 5,100 mg/day is above the labeled maximum, and I'm not able to enter a dose over that limit based on a confirmation I can't check.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label right now.** For example, 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n- **Route the above-label dose through pharmacy or the prescriber.** An above-maximum order generally needs direct prescriber entry, or pharmacist review with documented justification. That could be done through your hospital's override process.\n\nIf the specialist wants more glycemic control than metformin can give at its maximum, adding another agent is usually the next step. That decision belongs with the specialist.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter one of the in-label regimens."
      }
     ],
